   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HEALTH RESILIENT FUND</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Health Resilience Fund programme in Zimbabwe, implemented by UNICEF, aims to reduce maternal mortality, child mortality, teenage pregnancy, and increase potential for all children, adolescents and youth to thrive by 2025.  Activities include: training health personnel; support operations of health facilities, procurement and supply of medicines and commodities; strengthening primary and community health care systems; child immunization and care, strengthening demand and supply side for SRH &amp; nutrition services.</narrative>
  </description>
